[373.65,"o","We did a weak change to test: changed strictEqual import. Wait we still import strictEqual. Need\r\n  to use assert.strictEqual? In node:assert/strict provide strictEqual exported? Actually\r\n  assert.strictEqual is exported; but import { strictEqual } from 'node:assert/strict'; doesn't\r\n  exist. Instead import { strictEqual } from 'node:assert';? Let's verify: In Node v22, assert\r\n  module: exports.strictEqual function. Should be 'node:assert/strict', but export names: assert.\r\n  Let's check. We'll run a simple snippet? Probably easier: use import { strictEqual } from\r\n  'node:assert';. But test uses strictEqual. Let's use import { strictEqual } from 'node:assert';.\r\n  Let's edit accordingly."]
[373.65,"o","\r\n"]
[373.65,"o","\r\n\u001b[38;2;45;212;191m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(slug.test.mjs)\r\n"]
